{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-69653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-69653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $5$ and position $4$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $5$ and position $4$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 4 &  & 6 &  & 4 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 5 &  & 10 &  & 10 &  & 5 &  & 1 \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4})=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-69653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6810555fded97983c0b3ae1a6f9182e69a68a93d9e3785970dc8243dc21e1f45"} {"question" "q-69653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-69653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-69653" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-70307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{6}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-70307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{6}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-6)!\\cdot 6!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6!}{1!\\cdot 6!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot \\cancel{6!}}{1\\cdot \\cancel{6!}} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-70307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6810555fded97983c0b3ae1a6f9182e69a68a93d9e3785970dc8243dc21e1f45"} {"question" "q-70307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-70307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "42"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-70307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-70324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{8}{3}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-70324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=8$ and $r=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{8}{3}) & =\\frac{8!}{(8-3)!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{5!\\cdot 3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot \\cancel{6}\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}\\cdot \\cancel{6}} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-70324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6810555fded97983c0b3ae1a6f9182e69a68a93d9e3785970dc8243dc21e1f45"} {"question" "q-70324" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-70324" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "112"] ["math" "28"] ["math" "48"] ["math" "56"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"} {"question" "q-70324" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "56"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058437/state.json" "file_sha256" "f1c3d7a210c9a76bb54b58464011cc042f62d8e0d44f072aed54a4d7a3c0aba1"}] "usage" {"q-69653" []} "basis" 1879 "retractions" [[17592186172519 :question/problem "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\frac{5}{4})$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186171080 17592186171081 17592186171082 17592186171083 17592186171084] "immutable_fields" [[1759